+LPU Support Runbook — Generic Scaffold
+====================================
+
+Purpose
+-------
Provide operators with steps to enable and validate LPU support using the generic scaffold. This runbook assumes you will later fill vendor-specific compile commands and runtime installs.
+
+Prereqs
+- Host nodes with LPU devices attached and vendor drivers installed.
+- Kubernetes cluster access (kubectl) and permission to label nodes.
+- Repo checkout and python3 available on operator machine.
+
+Quick steps
+1. Install vendor runtime on host(s) (follow vendor docs). Example installers exist under ops/installers/* as templates.
+2. Label nodes:
+   ./ops/lpu/label_lpu_nodes.sh aegis/lpu generic
+3. Deploy host-access DaemonSet if you need privileged access to /dev:
+   kubectl apply -f k8s/deviceplugins/lpu-daemonset.yaml
+4. Compile model:
+   python ops/lpu/generic/lpu_compile.py --input path/to/model.tflite --outdir /opt/models --cmd "your-compile-cmd {input} -o {out}"
+   -> Produces compiled artifact and .prov.json provenance
+5. Deploy serving:
+   Use ops/lpu/generic/lpu_adapter.py deploy_serving to create a Deployment that schedules on aegis/lpu=generic:
+     python -c "from ops.lpu.generic.lpu_adapter import deploy_serving; deploy_serving('aegis/lpu-serve:latest','/opt/models')"
+6. Run smoke inference:
+   curl -X POST http://<service-ip>:8080/ -d '{"input":[...]}'
+7. Validate outputs:
+   - Run ops/lpu/ci/compare_inference.py against CPU baseline and LPU outputs (adapt compare script from ops/npu/ci)
+8. Sign & upload:
+   - Sign compiled artifact and evaluation with KMS (ops/governance/kms_sign_helper.py)
+   - Upload to evidence store via ops/evidence/s3_retention_uploader.py
+
+Acceptance criteria
+- Compiled artifact and provenance JSON exist.
+- Serving pod running on node labeled aegis/lpu=generic.
+- Inference outputs within tolerance vs CPU baseline for representative scenarios.
+- Latency (p99) meets target.
+- Signed artifact and evaluation uploaded and indexed.
+
+Notes & risks
+- Quantization drift: run larger scenario coverage to detect accuracy regressions.
+- Driver stability: monitor pods for OOM or device errors; enable vendor logs.
+- Security: do not store vendor keys in plain text; use Vault/KMS for secrets.
+
